-- title:
--   Change of basis from an embedding basis to the good family
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $r$ a natural number, and let $\Phi$ be a family context `FamCtx p r` for $p$; among its data is a family $t = \Phi.t$ of $r$ elements of $\overline{M}_{1\cdot p} :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the image of the level-$1\cdot p$ modular function field under coefficientwise base change, and among its axioms is `t_basis`, the assertion `IsEmbBasis (1 * p) t`: the family $t$ is linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and its $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-span is the Riemann–Roch space of the divisor $\deg_{\mathrm{emb}}(1\cdot p)\cdot \overline{\infty}$, that is, the space of $f$ with $v(f)\le \exp(D(v))$ at every place $v$. Let $s : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to \overline{M}_{1\cdot p}$ be a further family satisfying the same condition `IsEmbBasis (1 * p) s`. The conclusion is that for every index $i$,
--   $$s_i = \sum_{j} (\mathrm{linkMatrix}\,\Phi\,s\,h_s)_{ij}\cdot t_j,$$
--   with the scalar action of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, where `goodFamily Φ` is $t$ and the $(i,j)$ entry of `linkMatrix` is by definition the $j$-th coordinate of $s_i$, regarded as an element of the span of $t$, in the linearly independent family $t$.
--
--   This is the change-of-basis identity relating an arbitrary basis of the Riemann–Roch space attached to the embedding divisor on the modular curve of level $p$ to the distinguished good family carried by a family context, expressed through the link matrix. It is used in the comparison of the two component charts (at the cusp $\infty$ and at the cusp $0$) and in the archimedean size estimates for evaluation vectors of the good family.
